 by scripts/gen_adr_index.py and enforced current by a dedicated staleness gate (gen_adr_index.py --check in .github/actions/docs-gates/action.yml); the plan prescribes the wrong edit mechanism and omits the generator step and that gate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"faf26bba0e482e505","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope section (docs/adr/README.md index row 'if the index lists ADRs'; docs/adr/.numbers/0123 'new marker')","norm_id":"n578aa92330c2a6b3","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author hand-writes README index row / marker; it drifts from generator output; gen_adr_index.py --check fails in CI even though check_adr_numbers.py and make verify passed.","A stale README index lands because make verify (Makefile:456 runs only check_adr_numbers.py) never invokes the staleness gate."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In Scope and Acceptance Criteria, state that README.md and the marker are regenerated via `scripts/gen_adr_index.py` and add an AC that `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check` exits 0.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify (co-located with the severity vocabulary in section 3) how the agentic engine sets each finding's `decision` (block/advisory/indeterminate) from its `severity`, so finalize_verdict's `decision`-keyed blocking bucket is populated — or state that the engine writes `decision` directly and `severity` is cosmetic.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Section 4: 'maps field-by-field onto the findings shape plan_review/sidecar.py writes and orchestrator.finalize_verdict reads, so downstream readers need no change.'","Section 3: 'a `blocker` finding blocks; major, minor and trivial are advisory. Zero blockers is PASS'","orchestrator.py:356 `blocking = parts[\"blocking\"]` and :366 `if blocking: verdict = \"BLOCK\"` — the blocking bucket drives the verdict","orchestrator.py:296-299 the blocking bucket is populated from `f.get(\"decision\") == \"block\"`, not from severity","sidecar.py:630-631 persists `decision` and `severity` as SEPARATE fields","passes.py:7,17 the existing pipeline emits NO severity and computes decision/priority in Pass-2/Pass-3, which the single-agent agentic engine does not run"],"finding":"Section 4 claims the agentic finding maps field-by-field onto the sidecar/finalize_verdict shape with no downstream change, but finalize_verdict derives its blocking bucket from a finding's `decision` key (block/advisory/indeterminate), not from the `severity` field the agentic engine emits; the step converting per-finding `severity` into the `decision`/blocking partition is never specified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f188738ce23cd6808","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"ADR section 3 (Severity-to-verdict mapping) and section 4 (Finding schema mapping); orchestrator.finalize_verdict","norm_id":"nb18eda5c81b4a7e1","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An agentic run returns a finding with severity=\"blocker\" but no `decision` key: finalize_verdict's blocking bucket is empty, the verdict is PASS, and a plan the agent judged blocking is silently claimable.","A reviewer implements the agentic engine against section 4's 'no downstream change' and finds the severity never influences the verdict."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In section 3/4, add the explicit rule: severity==\"blocker\" ⇒ finding.decision=\"block\"; major/minor/trivial ⇒ decision=\"advisory\"; and name where this stamping happens (the agentic engine adapter) since no Pass-2/Pass-3 priority computation runs to set `decision`.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define how the agentic `criterion` value (including the literal `general`) maps to the downstream `criteria` list and what posture/verdict treatment `general` receives (e.g. always advisory) so registry-posture resolution is well-defined.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Section 4: 'extended with a `criterion` naming a registry criterion id or `general`'","orchestrator.py:325-330 blocking_ids are registry ids with default_posture==\"blocking\"; a finding's `criteria` list is intersected against them","sidecar.py:621 and finding shape use `criteria` (list), not `criterion` (singular string)","`general` is not a registry id, so its posture / verdict role is undefined"],"finding":"Section 4 introduces a `criterion` field whose value may be the literal `general`, but `general` is not a registry criterion id and the downstream blocking/criterion handling keys off `criteria` (a list) resolved against registry.by_id() default_posture; the vocabulary and name mismatch (singular `criterion` vs list `criteria`, plus the undefined `general` posture) is not reconciled.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbdac7a15f11f4440","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"ADR section 4 (Finding schema mapping)","norm_id":"n36d2f87457b3ef86","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A finding tagged criterion=\"general\": it matches no registry blocking id, so even a blocker-severity general finding never satisfies _any_blocking_criterion / posture-based routing, and its verdict handling is undefined.","An implementer must guess whether `criterion` is coerced into the `criteria` list and how `general` is treated for posture."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In section 2, attribute the `effort` knob to the sibling model-upgrade ticket (beaten-natural-grouse) rather than describing it as an already-existing RunRequest/config field.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.105,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["search of src/rebar/llm/runner.py and src/rebar/llm/config.py for 'effort' finds no RunRequest/LLMConfig field (only best-effort comments)","beaten-natural-grouse description: 'Effort, explicit. One per-model table beside the overrides ... build_model_settings and build_agent_kwargs send it through provider-scoped keys: bedrock_additional_model_requests_fields={\"output_config\": {\"effort\": ...}} ... anthropic_effort'"],"finding":"ADR section 2 claims budget/effort knobs including `effort high` are 'all existing RunRequest/config fields, no new knob', but no `effort` field currently exists on RunRequest (src/rebar/llm/runner.py) or LLMConfig (src/rebar/llm/config.py); the effort mechanism (per-model table, anthropic_effort / output_config.effort) is introduced by the linked sibling ticket beaten-natural-grouse, not pre-existing.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc6c436008afe5524","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section 2 'Agentic engine design' — 'effort high ... all existing RunRequest/config fields, no new knob'","norm_id":"nf189513f34a95b54","priority":0.595,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader of the ADR assumes effort is already a settable runner field and plans an engine child against it before beaten-natural-grouse lands the mechanism."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the `effort` setting with the actual code: either name the existing field/mechanism that carries reasoning effort (RunRequest/LLMConfig) with a line cite, or state that effort requires a NEW knob and drop the 'no new knob' claim in section 2.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.305,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Section 2: 'effort high, per-request timeout cfg.timeout_s — all existing RunRequest/config fields, no new knob.'","Section 7: 'with sampling parameters withdrawn and effort set explicitly (high for Opus and Sonnet, medium for Haiku)'","CONTRADICTED: repo-wide search of src/rebar/llm for `effort`, `reasoning_effort`, `reasoning`, and effort values `high`/`medium` finds no such field — RunRequest (runner.py:57-114) has iteration_limit/tool_step_limit/output_token_limit/thinking but no effort; LLMConfig (config.py ~350-374) exposes temperature, max_tokens, max_iterations, timeout_s but no effort; model_classes.py has no reasoning/effort knob.","By contrast the sibling budget knobs the plan names ARE verified: RunRequest.iteration_limit (runner.py:95), tool_step_limit (runner.py:102), output_token_limit (runner.py:96), cfg.timeout_s (config.py:355)."],"finding":"Section 2 ('effort high') and Section 7 ('effort set explicitly, high for Opus/Sonnet, medium for Haiku') assert the reasoning-`effort` setting is 'all existing RunRequest/config fields, no new knob' — but no `effort` (or reasoning-effort) field exists on RunRequest, LLMConfig, or the model classes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f440d32b775cc64da","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach, section 2 (Agentic engine design) 'effort high ... all existing RunRequest/config fields, no new knob'; and section 7 (Model upgrade) 'effort set explicitly (high for Opus and Sonnet, medium for Haiku)'","norm_id":"n00692f7acc1a4b91","priority":0.595,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A later child codes the agentic engine against section 2 expecting to pass `effort=\"high\"` through an existing field and finds none, forcing either a new config/RunRequest field (contradicting 'no new knob') or silently dropping the setting.","The model-upgrade child (beaten-natural-grouse) tries to 'set effort explicitly' per model and discovers there is no effort plumbing, scope-creeping the upgrade into a runner change."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"y